<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippine court halts waterworks privatisation.</title>
<headline>Philippine court halts waterworks privatisation.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine Court of Appeals on Friday said it had temporarily halted the privatisation of the Manila waterworks system in response to a petition by a group of people who said President Fidel Ramos did not have the authority to carry out the programme.</p>
<p>A three-judge panel of the court said the city's Metropolitan Water and Sewerage System (MWSS) was halted from any act furthering the privatisation of the utility until further orders. It also ordered the MWSS to respond to the petition within 10 days.</p>
<p>The ruling was issued on Thursday and announced on Friday.</p>
</text>
